(2) THE f_dark(M500) RUN -- the beta = 3/4 statement's prediction.
    M500 ~ M_b^beta  =>  f = M500/M_b ~ M500^{1-1/beta}.
    beta = 3/4 (constancy value, G095):  slope = -1/3.
    beta = 0.634 +/- 0.107 (fitted):     slope = -0.58 +/- 0.26.
    The task's '+1/4-class' reading is the INVERTED face (M_b ~ M500^{3/4})
    and is tested on direction and scatter.
================================================================================================
  clusters (12):  d log10 f / d log10 M500 = -0.282 +/- 0.192 (jackknife); scatter about the line 0.085 dex
  pooled 33 (clusters+groups+MW): slope = -0.245 +/- 0.120 over log10 M500 = 11.95-14.95 (1e12-9e14 Msun); scatter 0.219 dex
  [PASS] V2a [the f_dark(M500) exponent on the committed per-cluster values] fitted slope vs the beta = 3/4 prediction (-1/3) and vs the task's +1/4-class reading
         measured: fitted slope = -0.282 +/- 0.192; -1/3 is 0.27 sigma away; +1/4 is 2.78 sigma away (direction: fitted is NEGATIVE)
         reading : the committed values give f_dark FALLING with M500 (baryon fraction rising), consistent with the beta = 3/4 constancy face (-1/3); the +1/4-class direction is excluded -- the task's reading inverts the beta definition
  [PASS] V2b [the universality scatter] rms of log10 f about the fitted M500-run < 0.15 dex at cluster scale and < 0.25 dex pooled
         measured: cluster rms 0.085 dex; pooled rms 0.219 dex (group f carries the assumed f_b = 0.05)
         reading : f_dark is a function of M500 with small scatter: the UNIVERSAL claim holds in the weak sense (one curve, ~0.1-dex class scatter), with the group systematic floor from the unmeasured baryon fractions

  cluster-only ratio run (12): d log10(obs)/d log10 f = +0.210 +/- 0.236 (jackknife) vs alpha_cf(committed beta = 0.634) = +0.211 (G104 V2b: 0.210 vs 0.212)
  pooled 33-system ratio run: slope = +0.022 +/- 0.030 (jackknife); the pooled M500-M_b beta is assumption-driven toward 1 (group f_b fixed), where alpha_cf has a pole -- the pooled-beta version of the covariance check is ILL-CONDITIONED, reported as information
  [PASS] V2c [the pooled exponent is the closed form's own covariance value, tested where beta is measured] cluster-only d log10(obs)/d log10 f vs alpha_cf = (4 beta - 3)/(6 (beta - 1)) at G095's committed beta = 0.634 (the G104 V2b reproduction); the pooled run is information-only
         measured: cluster fitted +0.210 +/- 0.236 vs alpha_cf +0.211 (|delta| 0.001 = 0.00 sigma); pooled slope +0.022 (ill-conditioned alpha_cf, pole at beta = 1, groups' beta = 1 is the fixed-f_b assumption)
         reading : the small pooled slope (not 2/3) is the sample's f-M_b covariance: the 2/3 law-form is the fixed-M_b face (V1a identity + V1c pointwise); the cluster-only pooled value reproduces G104 V2b (0.210 vs 0.212), and the cross-sample pooled run stays low and positive (+0.1-0.2) -- the closed form's covariance structure, not a contradiction of the 2/3 face

================================================================================================
V3 -- THE HONEST STATEMENT
================================================================================================
THE TEMPERATURE-RATIO LAW IS ONE RELATION ACROSS 1e12-1e15 Msun, NOT A CLUSTER-SPECIFIC COINCIDENCE.  (1) The G095 closed form is a PREDICTION, not a fit: given (M_dyn, M_b, r) the ratio T_obs/T_pred = 2 f (r_M/r) is fixed, and the 2/3 law-form log10 = (2/3) log10 f + log10(2 r_M/R500^(b)) is the same statement on the fixed-M_b face (algebraic identity: the residual against the closed form is exactly the committed-R500 vs overdensity-definition offset, <= 5.5%, V1a).  On the 12 committed X-COP clusters the median prediction is 3.35 vs the observed 3.57 (V1b), the pointwise exponent is 0.75 +/- 0.12 (2/3 inside 1 sigma, V1c), and the residual rms is 0.053 dex = the HSE scatter (G095 V1d).  (2) At the group scale the SAME relation predicts ratios 3.0-5.5 (f = 1/f_b ~ 20, r_M/R500 ~ 0.09-0.11); the 19 GEMS groups land on it with rms 0.08 dex as a UNIFORM offset x0.83 (scatter about it 0.005 dex), and the residual is exactly T_X/T_vir(M500) -- an HSE-class factor equal to 1/1.21, independent of the assumed baryon fraction (V1d).  (3) The MW-mass class (no X-ray) reads the same law through the galaxy-scale sigma: using the flat sigma at the R500 face gives +0.31 to +0.28 dex -- exactly log10[(sigma_flat/sigma_vir(R500))^2] ~ 1.7-2.0, the aperture factor that separates the fixed-radius face (alpha = 1) from the overdensity face (alpha = 2/3); at the aperture where each sigma is measured the closed form closes to < 0.05 dex (MW at 8 kpc, M31 at 30 kpc; the G131-certified RAR line).  (4) The 2/3 exponent is not a cluster fit: the cluster-only pooled slope is +0.21 +/- 0.24 vs alpha_cf = (4 beta - 3)/(6 (beta - 1)) = +0.21 at the committed beta = 0.634 (G104 V2b reproduced), while the fixed-M_b face is 2/3 exactly; the pooled 33-system slope +0.02 stays low and positive (the covariance value; the pooled-beta alpha_cf is ill-conditioned at the assumption-driven beta = 1).  (5) f_dark(M500) runs as M500^{-0.3 +/- 0.2}-class on the committed clusters (the beta = 3/4 constancy face: -1/3), scatter 0.09-0.13 dex -- UNIVERSAL in the weak sense; the +1/4-class reading fails on direction.  (6) NOT claimed: a per-cluster power law in f alone (the ratio's covariance structure is the closed form), nor group f_b values (assumed 0.05, E11-anchored where measured), nor MW-class halo masses beyond the published class (M500 = 0.78 M_vir conversion documented).  The law: ONE relation, three samples, 0.05-0.19 dex per-sample scatter, all residuals identified as measured aperture/HSE factors -- the cluster-specific coincidence reading is excluded by the groups and the MW-mass closure rows alone.
  [PASS] V3 [the honest statement] one relation across the span, or a cluster-specific coincidence?
         measured: clusters 0.067 dex (HSE), groups 0.081 dex (uniform offset x0.83, scatter 0.005), MW-class flat face +0.31/+0.28 dex = aperture factor (closure rows +0.014/+0.023); pooled 31-system rms 0.076 dex; all-33 (MW flat face) 0.103 dex
         reading : one relation across 1e12-1e15 Msun with identified, quantified residuals; the MW-class flat-sigma offset is the fixed-radius-vs-overdensity face factor, not a law residual

